tate"},"272":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/adapters-45","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/adapters","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/adapters#support-matrix","content":"`@coaction/xstate`"},"273":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/adapters-46","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/adapters","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/adapters#support-matrix","content":"Supported"},"274":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/adapters-47","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/adapters","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/adapters#support-matrix","content":"Unsupported"},"275":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/adapters-48","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/adapters","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/adapters#support-matrix","content":"N/A"},"276":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/adapters-49","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/adapters","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/adapters#support-matrix","content":"Shared support means Coaction method execution is maintained. It does not promise that arbitrary\nout-of-band writes to every external runtime propagate across authority and client."},"277":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/adapters-50","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/adapters","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/adapters#zustand-example","content":"Use this path when the Zustand store must remain public API or other modules still consume it\ndirectly. For a new store owned by Coaction, prefer the native state model."},"278":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/adapters-51","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/adapters","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/adapters#mobx-example","content":"The external runtime owns its mutable object. Unknown root properties written directly onto a\nmutable adapter are not promoted into Coaction's fixed raw/public schema."},"279":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/adapters-52","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/adapters","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/adapters#pinia-jotai-redux-valtio-and-xstate","content":"These packages expose `bind*` helpers and, where needed, an `adapt()` wrapper:"},"280":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/adapters-53","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/adapters","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/adapters#pinia-jotai-redux-valtio-and-xstate","content":"XState blocks `setState()`; send actor events. Redux and XState are local-only maintained\ncontracts today."},"281":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/adapters-54","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/adapters","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/adapters#authoring-an-adapter","content":"Custom adapters import `defineExternalStoreAdapter()` from `coaction/adapter`. They must preserve\nthe core `Store` lifecycle, notify Coaction after direct external immutable writes, and declare\nsupport boundaries with contract tests. See contributing before\nstarting one."},"282":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/adapters-55","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/adapters","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/adapters#the-write-boundary","content":"`store.apply` belongs to Coaction. An adapter says how to write a change into\nits own runtime by setting `internal.externalApply`, and that is the whole of\nits job here — Coaction works out the patch pair, runs commit validators, calls\nthe writer, and publishes the commit."},"283":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/adapters-56","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/adapters","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/adapters#the-write-boundary","content":"An adapter that only wants to refuse a direct write, because its runtime takes\nchanges through its own channel, needs no writer at all — refuse from\n`internal.assertMutationAllowed` and let the ordinary `apply` do the work."},"284":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/adapters-57","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/adapters","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/adapters#the-write-boundary","content":"Adapters used to replace `store.apply` outright. That took on commit semantics\nthey did not want, and discarded anything middleware had wrapped `apply` with,\nsince middleware runs first."},"285":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks","type":"page","content":"Framework integrations","breadcrumbs":["Coaction","Integrations"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks"},"286":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks-0","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks","content":"Connect one Coaction store model to React, Vue, Angular, Svelte, or Solid."},"287":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks-1","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks#react","content":"React"},"288":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks-2","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks#whole-selectors","content":"Whole selectors"},"289":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks-3","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks#server-rendering","content":"Server rendering"},"290":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks-4","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks#vue","content":"Vue"},"291":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks-5","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks#angular","content":"Angular"},"292":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks-6","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks#svelte","content":"Svelte"},"293":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks-7","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks#solid","content":"Solid"},"294":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks-8","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks#shared-mode-note","content":"Shared-mode note"},"295":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks-9","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks","content":"Framework packages wrap the core `Store` contract with the reactive primitive native to each\necosystem. State creation, actions, computed getters, slices, and shared-mode rules remain core\nbehavior."},"296":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks-10","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks#react","content":"`@coaction/react` supports React 18 and 19. Both are covered by CI, which\ninstalls each and runs the suite against it."},"297":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks-11","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks#react","content":"Inside `observer()`, a no-selector hook call tracks fields read during render. Outside\n`observer()`, it is a whole-store subscription. Use an explicit selector when that intent is\nclearer:"},"298":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks-12","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks#react","content":"`<Observer>` creates a smaller tracked render region, and `useCounter.auto()` returns a cached\nfield-selector map."},"299":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks-13","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks#whole-selectors","content":"A selector that scans most of the state anyway gains little from tracking each read. Pass\n`{ whole: true }` to run it over the store's plain data instead:"},"300":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks-14","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks#whole-selectors","content":"A whole selector receives `getPureState()`: the store's own data as plain objects, without getters\nor methods. It records no dependencies, runs again on every commit, and re-renders the component\nonly when the result changes by `Object.is`, or by the `equals` you pass. While no tracked selector\nor `observer()` reads a store, its writes skip the patch bookkeeping that tracking needs."},"301":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks-15","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks#whole-selectors","content":"The selector is handed the store's own data: read it, never mutate it. Keep each hook call in one\nmode, since switching a call between `{ whole: true }` and a tracked selector changes the hooks it\nruns."},"302":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks-16","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks#server-rendering","content":"On a server there is nothing to subscribe to, so every way of reading a store is\na plain read of the state as it is at that moment — a selector, a no-selector\ncall, and `observer` all agree."},"303":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks-17","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks#server-rendering","content":"That matters when something has written to the store before rendering: a request\npreloading data, a hydration middleware, an initialisation second phase. All\nthree report the value that was written, which is also what the client hydrates\nagainst, so React accepts the markup instead of reporting a mismatch and\nre-rendering the tree."},"304":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks-18","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks#server-rendering","content":"If you want the value the store was created with, ask for it:"},"305":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks-19","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks#vue","content":"`useCounter({ autoSelector: true })` returns computed refs for known fields. Call methods directly\nand read data refs through `.value`."},"306":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks-20","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks#angular","content":"`select()` returns an Angular signal-like accessor for the selector result."},"307":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks-21","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks#svelte","content":"The selector call returns a readable Svelte store."},"308":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks-22","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks#solid","content":"The selector result is a Solid accessor."},"309":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks-23","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks#shared-mode-note","content":"Framework packages can wrap a client mirror. Store methods then return promises even if the same\nmethod is synchronous in a local store. Await mutations when the store is created with a Worker\nor SharedWorker."},"310":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks-24","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/frameworks#shared-mode-note","content":"Generated selector maps are based on the schema known during initialization. Dynamic paths\ninside a declared record should use an explicit selector rather than expecting an auto-selector\nmap to grow."},"311":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware","type":"page","content":"Logger, persist, and history","breadcrumbs":["Coaction","Integrations"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware"},"312":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware-0","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware","content":"Add diagnostics, persistence, and undo/redo to a Coaction-owned store through middleware."},"313":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware-1","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware#logger","content":"Logger"},"314":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware-2","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware#persist","content":"Persist"},"315":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware-3","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware#history","content":"History"},"316":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware-4","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware#shared-placement","content":"Shared placement"},"317":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware-5","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware","content":"Middleware receives the store during creation and may decorate its methods or attach an API. Pass\nmiddleware in array order through the plural `middlewares` option."},"318":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware-6","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware#logger","content":"You may inject a console-compatible logger. Serialized mode safely handles circular diagnostic\nvalues and BigInt; logging does not weaken the shared JSON contract."},"319":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware-7","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware#logger","content":"Install logger on the authority for authority-side action and patch diagnostics. A client logger\nis limited to mirrored updates and proxied calls."},"320":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware-8","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware#persist","content":"The default storage is `localStorage` when available. `createJSONStorage()` adapts another Web\nStorage instance, and a custom `PersistStorage` may be synchronous or asynchronous."},"321":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware-9","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware#persist","content":"`persist()` attaches:"},"322":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware-10","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware#persist","content":"If a payload contains an explicit version that differs from the configured version, provide\n`migrate`. Without it, hydration is skipped and `onRehydrateStorage` receives the error."},"323":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware-11","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware#persist","content":"`merge` output still obeys the fixed schema: unknown root keys are rejected."},"324":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware-12","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware#history","content":"`partialize` limits which state participates in time travel. `limit` must be a non-negative\ninteger."},"325":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware-13","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware#shared-placement","content":"Middleware"},"326":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware-14","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware#shared-placement","content":"Local"},"327":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware-15","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware#shared-placement","content":"Shared main"},"328":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware-16","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware#shared-placement","content":"Shared client"},"329":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware-17","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware#shared-placement","content":"Logger"},"330":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware-18","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware#shared-placement","content":"Supported"},"331":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware-19","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware#shared-placement","content":"Supported"},"332":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware-20","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware#shared-placement","content":"Limited visibility"},"333":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware-21","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware#shared-placement","content":"Persist"},"334":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware-22","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware#shared-placement","content":"Supported"},"335":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware-23","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware#shared-placement","content":"Supported"},"336":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware-24","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware#shared-placement","content":"Rejected"},"337":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware-25","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware#shared-placement","content":"History"},"338":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware-26","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware#shared-placement","content":"Supported"},"339":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware-27","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware#shared-placement","content":"Supported"},"340":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware-28","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware#shared-placement","content":"Rejected"},"341":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware-29","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware#shared-placement","content":"Persistence and time travel are writes. Put them on the authority store so every client observes\none result. Never present client-local persistence or undo as authoritative state."},"342":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware-30","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/middleware#shared-placement","content":"`persist` and `history` coordinate so hydration does not create misleading undo entries."},"343":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync","type":"page","content":"Local-first sync","breadcrumbs":["Coaction","Integrations"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/integrations/sync"},"344":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync-0","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/sync","content":"Keep a Coaction store working offline and converging with a server, through a durable outbox and a rebase."},"345":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync-1","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/integrations/sync#reading-the-queue","content":"Reading the queue"},"346":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync-2","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/integrations/sync#backends","content":"Backends"},"347":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync-3","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/integrations/sync#conflicts","content":"Conflicts"},"348":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync-4","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/integrations/sync#state-has-to-be-json","content":"State has to be JSON"},"349":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync-5","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/integrations/sync#storage","content":"Storage"},"350":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync-6","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/integrations/sync#delivery","content":"Delivery"},"351":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync-7","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/sync","content":"`@coaction/sync` is middleware. The store stays an ordinary Coaction store —\nactions, selectors, `observer`, history — and every commit it makes is also\nqueued for a server."},"352":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync-8","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/sync","content":"A write lands locally at once. It is written to a durable outbox before anything\nis sent, so a crash between the write and the delivery is recoverable, and a\npull rebases whatever is still pending over what the server sent."},"353":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync-9","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/sync","content":"This is not shared authority. A synced store owns\nits state and reconciles with a remote; a shared store's mirrors are views of\none authority in another JavaScript context. They compose, and neither implies\nthe other."},"354":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync-10","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/sync#reading-the-queue","content":"`getPending()` hands back copies. The queue is what the client owes the server\nand the rebase reads it back as its own working set, so nothing outside can edit\nit by accident."},"355":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync-11","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/sync#backends","content":"Import"},"356":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync-12","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/sync#backends","content":"Backend"},"357":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync-13","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/sync#backends","content":"`@coaction/sync`"},"358":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync-14","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/sync#backends","content":"`createFetchSyncAdapter` — JSON over HTTP"},"359":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync-15","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/sync#backends","content":"`@coaction/sync/crud`"},"360":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync-16","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/sync#backends","content":"`createCrudSyncAdapter` — a record-shaped API"},"361":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync-17","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/sync#backends","content":"`@coaction/sync/supabase`"},"362":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync-18","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/sync#backends","content":"a Postgres table, with an optional changes-since cursor and realtime"},"363":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync-19","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/sync#backends","content":"`@coaction/sync/firestore`"},"364":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync-20","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/sync#backends","content":"a Firestore collection or query, with optional `onSnapshot`"},"365":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync-21","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/sync#backends","content":"`@coaction/sync/query`"},"366":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync-22","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/sync#backends","content":"TanStack Query"},"367":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync-23","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/sync#backends","content":"An adapter is two functions, so a backend not listed here is a `pull` and a\n`push`:"},"368":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync-24","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/sync#backends","content":"`push` returns the ids the remote durably accepted. Anything it does not\nacknowledge stays queued and is retried."},"369":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync-25","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/sync#conflicts","content":"When a pull brings a change that overlaps something still pending, the default\nkeeps the local write. `conflict: 'remote-wins'` keeps the remote one, and a\nfunction decides per mutation:"},"370":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync-26","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/sync#conflicts","content":"Each call is given its own copy of everything, so a resolver that works on what\nit is handed cannot disturb the rebase or the next call."},"371":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync-27","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/sync#state-has-to-be-json","content":"The outbox, the optimistic snapshot and the adapter's view of the remote are all\nstored as JSON, so state JSON cannot represent is not persisted — it is quietly\nchanged. A `Date` comes back a string; a `Map` comes back `{}`."},"372":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync-28","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/sync#state-has-to-be-json","content":"A write that introduces one is refused **before it is committed**, so the error\nreaches the caller and the store keeps state it can carry. Keep dates as ISO\nstrings or epoch numbers, keyed collections as records, and sets as arrays."},"373":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync-29","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/sync#state-has-to-be-json","content":"`sync()` does not attach to an external mutable adapter — MobX, Valtio and Pinia\nexpose accessor-backed state, which this contract refuses when the store is\nbuilt."},"374":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync-30","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/sync#storage","content":"Defaults to `localStorage`. Pass a `storage`, or\n`@coaction/sync/indexeddb` for a larger durable store:"},"375":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync-31","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/sync#storage","content":"There is no silent fallback to memory: a runtime with nowhere durable to write\nis refused, because the outbox surviving a crash is the reason it exists."},"376":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync-32","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/sync#delivery","content":"Mutations are delivered **at least once**. The window between the remote\ncommitting a write and the acknowledgement reaching durable storage cannot be\nclosed from the client, so a crash inside it means the restart sends that\nmutation again. Treat mutation `id` values idempotently."},"377":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync-33","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/sync#delivery","content":"The package README\ncovers the durable checkpoint format, what each built-in adapter guarantees\nunder replay, and the CRUD baseline."},"378":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/yjs","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/yjs","type":"page","content":"Yjs collaboration","breadcrumbs":["Coaction","Integrations"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/integrations/yjs"},"379":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/yjs-0","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/yjs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/yjs","content":"Bind Coaction-owned pure state to a Y.Doc and let a Yjs provider handle peer transport."},"380":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/yjs-1","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/yjs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/integrations/yjs#middleware-setup","content":"Middleware setup"},"381":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/yjs-2","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/yjs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/integrations/yjs#use-an-existing-ydoc","content":"Use an existing Y.Doc"},"382":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/yjs-3","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/yjs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/integrations/yjs#storage-and-sync-model","content":"Storage and sync model"},"383":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/yjs-4","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/yjs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/integrations/yjs#conflict-semantics","content":"Conflict semantics"},"384":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/yjs-5","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/yjs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/integrations/yjs#requirements-and-limits","content":"Requirements and limits"},"385":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/yjs-6","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/yjs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/yjs","content":"`@coaction/yjs` synchronizes a Coaction store's pure data with Yjs. It does not provide a network\nconnection; choose `y-websocket`, `y-webrtc`, or another Yjs provider for peer transport."},"386":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/yjs-7","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/yjs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/yjs#middleware-setup","content":"The middleware creates a `Y.Doc`, binds the store, and connects cleanup to `store.destroy()`."},"387":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/yjs-8","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/yjs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/yjs#use-an-existing-ydoc","content":"`bindYjs()` returns the `doc`, root `map`, `syncNow()`, and `destroy()`."},"388":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/yjs-9","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/yjs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/yjs#storage-and-sync-model","content":"State lives under `doc.getMap(key).get('state')`."},"389":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/yjs-10","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/yjs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/yjs#storage-and-sync-model","content":"Nested objects and arrays become nested `Y.Map` and `Y.Array` structures."},"390":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/yjs-11","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/yjs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/yjs#storage-and-sync-model","content":"Local Coaction changes are diffed against the last synchronized snapshot."},"391":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/yjs-12","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/yjs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/yjs#storage-and-sync-model","content":"Remote Yjs updates are replayed into Coaction."},"392":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/yjs-13","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/yjs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/yjs#storage-and-sync-model","content":"Methods and computed getters are not part of the synchronized payload."},"393":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/yjs-14","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/yjs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/yjs#storage-and-sync-model","content":"The default key is `coaction:${store.name}`."},"394":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/yjs-15","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/yjs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/yjs#conflict-semantics","content":"Concurrent edits to different fields can merge through Yjs. Conflicts on the same scalar field\nfollow Yjs semantics, effectively last-writer-wins for that value. When an operation must be\ncommutative—such as a distributed counter—model that field with a CRDT-native Yjs structure or\noperation instead of repeatedly replacing a scalar."},"395":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/yjs-16","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/yjs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/yjs#requirements-and-limits","content":"Keep synchronized state plain and serializable."},"396":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/yjs-17","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/yjs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/yjs#requirements-and-limits","content":"Yjs binding is supported on local and shared-main stores, not shared clients."},"397":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/yjs-18","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/yjs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/yjs#requirements-and-limits","content":"Bind the owning store only; a client mirror must not create a second collaboration authority."},"398":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/yjs-19","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/yjs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/yjs#requirements-and-limits","content":"Very large or highly volatile trees can generate substantial update traffic."},"399":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/yjs-20","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/yjs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/yjs#requirements-and-limits","content":"Always release old bindings to prevent duplicate observers and stale writes."},"400":{"id":"/en/docs/integrations/yjs-21","page_id":"/en/docs/integrations/yjs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/integrations/yjs#requirements-and-limits","content":"Remote snapshots and deletes still follow Coaction's fixed schema. Unknown root keys are rejected;\nknown single-store fields may become `undefined` if absent from an exact replacement."},"401":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand","type":"page","content":"Migrate from Zustand","breadcrumbs":["Coaction","Guides"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand"},"402":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand-0","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand","content":"Move an existing store incrementally while keeping selectors, middleware, and worker adoption deliberate."},"403":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand-1","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand#1-start-locally","content":"1\\. Start locally"},"404":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand-2","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand#2-keep-selectors-first","content":"2\\. Keep selectors first"},"405":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand-3","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand#3-move-repeated-derived-state-into-getters","content":"3\\. Move repeated derived state into getters"},"406":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand-4","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand#4-decide-whether-namespaced-slices-help","content":"4\\. Decide whether namespaced slices help"},"407":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand-5","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand#5-replace-middleware-separately","content":"5\\. Replace middleware separately"},"408":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand-6","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand#6-keep-zustand-underneath-when-that-is-safer","content":"6\\. Keep Zustand underneath when that is safer"},"409":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand-7","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand#7-add-shared-mode-last","content":"7\\. Add shared mode last"},"410":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand-8","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand#checklist","content":"Checklist"},"411":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand-9","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand","content":"Coaction deliberately keeps a familiar `create()` shape, but a migration is more than changing\nan import. Move one behavior at a time and keep tests green between steps."},"412":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand-10","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand#1-start-locally","content":"Do not begin by moving the store into a worker. First reproduce the current local behavior:"},"413":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand-11","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand#1-start-locally","content":"Zustand updaters usually return a partial object. Coaction also accepts object merges, but its\nnative path is a draft callback inside `set()`."},"414":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand-12","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand#2-keep-selectors-first","content":"Existing selector-oriented components can keep the explicit style:"},"415":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand-13","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand#2-keep-selectors-first","content":"It reads like Zustand's, and does less work. The selector runs inside a reactive tracker, so the\npaths it reads become its dependencies and a write touching none of them does not re-run it --\nwhere Zustand runs every selector on every store notification and compares the result.\n`Object.is` still decides the re-render in both. A familiar and low-risk migration point either\nway."},"416":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand-14","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand#2-keep-selectors-first","content":"Once the store is stable, use `observer()` where automatic read tracking removes meaningful\nselector boilerplate:"},"417":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand-15","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand#3-move-repeated-derived-state-into-getters","content":"Accessor getters are cached. Use `get(deps, selector)` only when explicit dependencies make the\ncode clearer."},"418":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand-16","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand#4-decide-whether-namespaced-slices-help","content":"Zustand's common slice pattern spreads factories into one flat object. Coaction native slices\nare namespaced:"},"419":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand-17","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand#4-decide-whether-namespaced-slices-help","content":"Do not convert solely to preserve the word “slice.” Keep a single store when the flat shape is\nclearer."},"420":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand-18","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand#5-replace-middleware-separately","content":"Zustand concern"},"421":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand-19","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand#5-replace-middleware-separately","content":"Coaction path"},"422":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand-20","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand#5-replace-middleware-separately","content":"Immer update middleware"},"423":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand-21","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand#5-replace-middleware-separately","content":"Built-in draft updates through `set()`"},"424":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand-22","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand#5-replace-middleware-separately","content":"Persist"},"425":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand-23","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand#5-replace-middleware-separately","content":"`@coaction/persist` on the owning store"},"426":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand-24","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand#5-replace-middleware-separately","content":"Selector subscriptions"},"427":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand-25","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand#5-replace-middleware-separately","content":"Framework selectors or automatic tracking"},"428":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand-26","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand#5-replace-middleware-separately","content":"Existing external Zustand runtime"},"429":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand-27","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand#5-replace-middleware-separately","content":"`@coaction/zustand` whole-store adapter"},"430":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand-28","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand#5-replace-middleware-separately","content":"Custom external runtime"},"431":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand-29","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand#5-replace-middleware-separately","content":"`defineExternalStoreAdapter()` from `coaction/adapter`"},"432":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand-30","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand#5-replace-middleware-separately","content":"Coaction does not currently promise a Redux DevTools-compatible built-in experience. Keep\nproject-specific diagnostics or use logger until a maintained DevTools surface exists."},"433":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand-31","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand#6-keep-zustand-underneath-when-that-is-safer","content":"Use `@coaction/zustand` when the existing Zustand store is itself public API, other modules\ndepend on it directly, or replacing ownership would create more risk than value. The adapter is a\nwhole-store integration; it cannot live inside native Coaction slices."},"434":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand-32","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand#7-add-shared-mode-last","content":"After local tests pass, create the same source on a worker authority and connect a client.\nSwitch the `create` import to the shared entry; the default React entry rejects worker options:"},"435":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand-33","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand#7-add-shared-mode-last","content":"Audit the state against the strict JSON contract and change call sites to await actions. Direct\nclient `setState()` is not a supported migration shortcut."},"436":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand-34","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand#checklist","content":"Keep explicit selectors during the first behavior-preserving step."},"437":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand-35","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand#checklist","content":"Move writes into `set()` and keep the root schema stable."},"438":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand-36","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand#checklist","content":"Convert repeated derived selectors into cached getters selectively."},"439":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand-37","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand#checklist","content":"Choose namespaced slices only when they improve ownership."},"440":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand-38","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand#checklist","content":"Replace persistence/history/logging one at a time."},"441":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand-39","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand#checklist","content":"Keep the existing Zustand runtime through the adapter when appropriate."},"442":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand-40","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/from-zustand#checklist","content":"Introduce workers only after local behavior and serialization are verified."},"443":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4","type":"page","content":"Migrating to 4.0","breadcrumbs":["Coaction","Guides"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4"},"444":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4-0","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4","content":"Update shared imports, check integration contracts, keep local React applications on supported versions, and check the Mutative 2 changes of 4.1 and the array element changes of 4.2."},"445":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4-1","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4#select-the-owning-entry","content":"Select the owning entry"},"446":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4-2","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4#check-low-level-writes-and-middleware","content":"Check low-level writes and middleware"},"447":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4-3","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4#check-react-and-computed-assumptions","content":"Check React and computed assumptions"},"448":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4-4","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4#check-remote-synchronization","content":"Check remote synchronization"},"449":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4-5","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4#check-mutative-2-in-41","content":"Check Mutative 2 in 4.1"},"450":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4-6","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4#check-array-elements-and-getinitialstate-in-42","content":"Check array elements and `getInitialState()` in 4.2"},"451":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4-7","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4","content":"Native local applications using actions, selectors and getters generally keep the same APIs.\nUse React 18 or 19, and check imports wherever state crosses a JavaScript context.\nThe repository migration guide\ncontains the extended adapter and local graph contracts."},"452":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4-8","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4#select-the-owning-entry","content":"Usage"},"453":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4-9","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4#select-the-owning-entry","content":"4.0 import"},"454":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4-10","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4#select-the-owning-entry","content":"Vanilla local store"},"455":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4-11","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4#select-the-owning-entry","content":"`coaction`"},"456":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4-12","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4#select-the-owning-entry","content":"Vanilla shared authority or client"},"457":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4-13","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4#select-the-owning-entry","content":"`coaction/shared`"},"458":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4-14","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4#select-the-owning-entry","content":"React local store"},"459":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4-15","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4#select-the-owning-entry","content":"`@coaction/react`"},"460":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4-16","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4#select-the-owning-entry","content":"React shared authority or client"},"461":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4-17","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4#select-the-owning-entry","content":"`@coaction/react/shared`"},"462":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4-18","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4#select-the-owning-entry","content":"Integration and commit hooks"},"463":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4-19","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4#select-the-owning-entry","content":"`coaction/adapter`"},"464":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4-20","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4#select-the-owning-entry","content":"Managed derived selectors and paths"},"465":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4-21","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4#select-the-owning-entry","content":"`coaction/derived`"},"466":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4-22","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4#select-the-owning-entry","content":"The old `coaction/local` and `@coaction/react/local` aliases are gone. Shared stores that\npreviously used a default entry must switch to `/shared`:"},"467":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4-23","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4#select-the-owning-entry","content":"The default entries reject non-null shared options such as `worker`, `transport` and\n`clientTransport`. An explicitly undefined option is accepted for feature detection and SSR.\nLocal imports exclude the shared transport runtime from the bundle."},"468":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4-24","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4#check-low-level-writes-and-middleware","content":"Both `store.apply(nextState)` and `store.apply(base, patches)` publish commits. With patches,\nthe base must be current: omit it with `apply(undefined, patches)` or use `getPureState()`.\nA wrong base throws before changing state or publishing a commit."},"469":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4-25","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4#check-low-level-writes-and-middleware","content":"Adapter authors must leave `store.apply` owned by Coaction and provide\n`internal.externalApply` for their runtime writer. Middleware should use\nStoreCommit hooks to observe all supported transitions,\nincluding writes that do not pass through `apply`."},"470":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4-26","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4#check-low-level-writes-and-middleware","content":"Do not assume every patch pair contains leaf paths. Positional edits can fall back to\nreplacement patches at changed top-level keys; local object graphs can need a root snapshot\nat `path: []`. Replay must preserve the committed values and reference topology.\nLocal cycles are supported as complete values during initialization or replacement. Creating\ncycles from draft references and editing within cyclic drafts remain outside the recipe\ncontract. These local guarantees do not extend the shared JSON contract."},"471":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4-27","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4#check-react-and-computed-assumptions","content":"React 18 and 19 are supported and tested. React 17 is outside the peer range.\nServer-side selectors read current state, consistent with whole-state and observer readers.\nUse `getInitialState()` explicitly if initial state is what the application needs, and create\nrequest-scoped stores with matching server and client hydration data."},"472":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4-28","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4#check-react-and-computed-assumptions","content":"Native getters retain store/slice field dependencies. React selectors and `observer` use deep\npath tracking; `derive(..., { deep: true })` opts a managed computed selector into deep tracking.\nSee computed state for identity, lifecycle and invalidation boundaries."},"473":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4-29","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4#check-remote-synchronization","content":"`@coaction/sync` requires durable storage and JSON state. Unsupported local writes are refused\nbefore committing. Checkpoints include `formatVersion`; unsupported versions and malformed\ncheckpoints are rejected without overwriting them. Legacy checkpoints without a version are\nread as format 1."},"474":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4-30","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4#check-remote-synchronization","content":"Review the CRUD, Supabase and Firestore adapter READMEs when upgrading those integrations:\nthe CRUD adapter retains the remote base, Supabase applies the configured schema to reads and\nwrites, and Firestore separates its read source from its write address. See\nremote synchronization for configuration and failure handling."},"475":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4-31","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4#check-remote-synchronization","content":"Reactive tracking, shared authority and remote synchronization are separate capabilities.\nA local store can sync to a server without a Worker. Shared mirrors follow one authority;\nthey do not independently diverge and merge like remote replicas."},"476":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4-32","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4#check-mutative-2-in-41","content":"Coaction 4.1 depends on Mutative 2, and\n`@coaction/history` on Travels 3, which declares Mutative 2 as its peer. No Coaction API changed.\nUpgrade `mutative` too if the application imports it, and replace libraries that declare\nMutative 1 as their peer, such as `zustand-mutative` 1, because npm stops with `ERESOLVE` next\nto `@coaction/history`."},"477":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4-33","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4#check-mutative-2-in-41","content":"Commit patches follow Mutative 2: nested patches come before their parents, and a moved draft\nis carried by the patches of its parent. They replay to the same state, so only tests that\ncompare patch arrays need new expectations. In production, errors from Mutative read\n`Minified Mutative error #<code>`; match the code, and define `process.env.NODE_ENV` in every\nbundle. The repository guide\ncovers loading without a bundler and the draft checks of development builds."},"478":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4-34","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4#check-array-elements-and-getinitialstate-in-42","content":"Coaction 4.2 hands array elements out as frozen values instead of readonly proxies. A reader\ndepends on the identity of each element it reads, so an `observer()` rendering `todos[0].title`\nre-renders after any write inside `todos[0]`, and read-only array methods such as `filter` take\none dependency on the array, even when they stop early, as `find` and `at` do. Where a component renders more often than before, read the field or\nthe scan's result through a selector, which re-renders only when its result changes. Objects\nreached through object keys are tracked as before."},"479":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4-35","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/migrating-to-v4#check-array-elements-and-getinitialstate-in-42","content":"A write to an element outside `set()` throws the engine's `TypeError` in strict-mode code and is\nsilently ignored in sloppy-mode scripts, instead of throwing Coaction's direct-mutation error.\n`getInitialState()` returns a copy of the initial state shaped like the factory's object, the\nsame object on every call, rather than the factory's object itself. `@coaction/react` adds opt-in\nwhole selectors, `useStore(selector, { whole: true })`, whose selector receives the store's own\ndata and must never mutate it. An array's state is its elements: `create()` and `setState({ ... })`\nleave out its named keys and symbols, as a recipe's first write to it always did, and warn once in\ndevelopment, so keep such a value in an object beside the array. The\nrepository guide\ncompares each change with 4.1."},"480":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/performance","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/performance","type":"page","content":"Performance and bundle boundaries","breadcrumbs":["Coaction","Guides"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guides/performance"},"481":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/performance-0","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/performance","content":"Interpret Coaction benchmarks honestly and keep local applications on the transport-free entry point."},"482":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/performance-1","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/performance","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guides/performance#choose-the-local-entry-point","content":"Choose the local entry point"},"483":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/performance-2","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/performance","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guides/performance#run-the-maintained-checks","content":"Run the maintained checks"},"484":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/performance-3","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/performance","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guides/performance#understand-the-derived-state-tradeoff","content":"Understand the derived-state tradeoff"},"485":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/performance-4","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/performance","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guides/performance#render-performance","content":"Render performance"},"486":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/performance-5","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/performance","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guides/performance#practical-checklist","content":"Practical checklist"},"487":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/performance-6","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/performance","content":"Performance claims are useful only when the scenario, runtime, state shape, and package versions\nare visible. Coaction keeps its benchmark scripts in the repository so results can be regenerated\ninstead of treated as timeless numbers."},"488":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/performance-7","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/performance#choose-the-local-entry-point","content":"For a vanilla local store:"},"489":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/performance-8","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/performance#choose-the-local-entry-point","content":"This static boundary excludes shared protocol, epoch, reconnect, and transport modules from the\nentry. Use `coaction/shared` for the shared runtime, or `@coaction/react/shared` in React.\nThe default React entry, `@coaction/react`, also stays local."},"490":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/performance-9","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/performance#choose-the-local-entry-point","content":"Bundle budgets in the repository measure published entries and tree-shaken consumer fixtures.\nThey are regression gates, not a promise that an application bundle equals the budget number;\nthe final result also depends on external dependencies retained by the application's bundler."},"491":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/performance-10","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/performance#run-the-maintained-checks","content":"`package:size` checks published entry budgets and core entry isolation."},"492":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/performance-11","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/performance#run-the-maintained-checks","content":"`benchmark` compares large update paths, including Coaction draft updates and Zustand + Immer."},"493":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/performance-12","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/performance#run-the-maintained-checks","content":"`benchmark:zustand-positioning` separates stable derived reads from update-then-read work."},"494":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/performance-13","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/performance#run-the-maintained-checks","content":"`benchmark:check` enforces regression floors with CI headroom."},"495":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/performance-14","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/performance#run-the-maintained-checks","content":"`benchmark:derived` runs built-entry workloads in fresh processes: sparse paths,\nrelated/unrelated writes, full scans, cached reads, and unread/disposed owners.\nIt is included in `benchmark:check`; full deep scans are reported to make their\ntracking cost visible, while native getters provide the coarse scan baseline."},"496":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/performance-15","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/performance#run-the-maintained-checks","content":"Thresholds must not be lowered merely to make a failing run green. A threshold change needs a\nreviewed runtime-semantic or benchmark-methodology reason."},"497":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/performance-16","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/performance#understand-the-derived-state-tradeoff","content":"Cached accessors make repeated stable reads extremely cheap. After an update, Coaction still must\npreserve the readonly public-state boundary and update the snapshot used by computed traversal.\nThat makes “update then read a derived value” a different path from a stable cached read."},"498":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/performance-17","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/performance#understand-the-derived-state-tradeoff","content":"Leave `enablePatches` unset unless an integration explicitly needs a journal. Commit hooks,\nshared transport and some tracking paths request patches automatically. Eligible small read\nsets can instead compare observed values before and after a write without generating patches;\ncached getter snapshots, patch middleware and larger dependency sets retain the patch path.\nOrdinary `subscribe()` listeners do not request patches themselves."},"499":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/performance-18","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/performance#understand-the-derived-state-tradeoff","content":"Do not publish one of those cases as a universal “faster than Zustand” claim. Zustand can make a\nderived read constant-time by storing the derived value, but application actions must then keep it\nconsistent. Coaction's proposition is maintained cached derivation, not winning every mutation\nmicrobenchmark."},"500":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/performance-19","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/performance#render-performance","content":"Both `useStore(selector)` and `observer()` use managed deep path tracking on native immutable\nstores. A reader of `state.user.name` can stay cached after an age-only recipe update. Selectors\nstill compare their results with `Object.is`; `observer()` collects reads during render without\nrequiring a selector. Measure selector executions and render counts separately."},"501":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/performance-20","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/performance#render-performance","content":"Array elements are values: a reader depends on the identity of each element it reads, and array\nmethods such as `filter` and `map` take one dependency on the array. An `observer()` rendering\n`todos[0].title` re-renders after any write inside `todos[0]`, and one rendering a scan after a\nwrite to any element. A selector returning the field or the scan's result reruns, but re-renders\nonly when that result changes."},"502":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/performance-21","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/performance#render-performance","content":"Native getters and `get(deps, fn)` retain the store/slice field boundary. A getter reading\n`this.user.name` can recompute when `user.age` changes, even if its result stays equal and its\nconsumers do no extra work. Use `derive(..., { deep: true })` or `derivePath` when a managed\nderived read needs finer dependencies."},"503":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/performance-22","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/performance#render-performance","content":"Parent replacement, array structure changes and graph snapshot patches can invalidate more\nbroadly. External adapters follow their own update and snapshot contracts. See\ncomputed tracking granularity for the boundaries."},"504":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/performance-23","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/performance#practical-checklist","content":"Import `coaction` for vanilla local-only state."},"505":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/performance-24","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/performance#practical-checklist","content":"Leave `enablePatches` unset unless needed; account for consumers that request patches automatically."},"506":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/performance-25","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/performance#practical-checklist","content":"Use cached getters for repeated derived reads, not side-effectful work."},"507":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/performance-26","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/performance#practical-checklist","content":"Use `observer()` where it removes real selector composition."},"508":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/performance-27","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/performance#practical-checklist","content":"Read a field of an array element, or the result of a scan, through a selector where an\n`observer()` would re-render for writes elsewhere in the elements."},"509":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/performance-28","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/performance#practical-checklist","content":"Profile production builds and representative state, not development mode alone."},"510":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/performance-29","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/performance#practical-checklist","content":"Treat benchmark floors as regression detection and rerun publishable numbers on the target\nmachine."},"511":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use","type":"page","content":"When not to use Coaction","breadcrumbs":["Coaction","Guides"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use"},"512":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use-0","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use","content":"An honest boundary check — the situations where Coaction is the wrong tool, and where it has no real competitor."},"513":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use-1","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use#skip-coaction-when","content":"Skip Coaction when"},"514":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use-2","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use#plain-single-tab-state-is-all-you-have","content":"Plain single-tab state is all you have"},"515":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use-3","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use#your-shared-state-is-not-json-shaped","content":"Your shared state is not JSON-shaped"},"516":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use-4","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use#call-sites-cannot-await-actions","content":"Call sites cannot await actions"},"517":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use-5","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use#your-measured-update-hot-path-misses-its-budget","content":"Your measured update hot path misses its budget"},"518":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use-6","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use#you-need-an-ecosystem-that-already-exists","content":"You need an ecosystem that already exists"},"519":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use-7","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use#your-browser-matrix-punishes-sharedworker","content":"Your browser matrix punishes SharedWorker"},"520":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use-8","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use#reach-for-coaction-when","content":"Reach for Coaction when"},"521":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use-9","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use#a-rule-of-thumb","content":"A rule of thumb"},"522":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use-10","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use","content":"Most apps do not need Coaction. A Zustand or Jotai store plus a few selectors is a smaller,\nsafer dependency for plain client state, and \"more powerful\" is not a reason to pay switching\ncosts. This page exists so you can make that call quickly, and so the cases where Coaction\ngenuinely has no equivalent are easy to find."},"523":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use-11","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use","content":"This guide is deliberately anti-marketing. If your situation is listed under \"skip it\", skip it —\nthe Coaction you would need is not the Coaction being offered."},"524":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use-12","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use#plain-single-tab-state-is-all-you-have","content":"A form here, a counter there, one settings panel. Coaction's readonly state and reactive runtime\nmay cost more than those needs justify. The default `coaction` and `@coaction/react` entries\nexclude the shared transport runtime; using a local store does not bundle an inactive transport.\n**Consider Zustand, Jotai, or component state** when their smaller model covers the problem.\nCoaction's local runtime becomes useful when shared derivation or read tracking removes\nsubstantial application code, even if the application never needs a Worker."},"525":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use-13","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use#your-shared-state-is-not-json-shaped","content":"Everything crossing a shared boundary — state, action arguments, returned values — must be a\nplain JSON tree: no `Date`, no `Map`, no class instances, no `undefined`, no cycles. Domain\nmodels built from rich objects need a serialization redesign before they can be shared, and\nthat redesign is the real cost, not the store call. Keep such state local, or accept the mapping\nlayer. See the JSON contract for the exact rules."},"526":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use-14","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use#call-sites-cannot-await-actions","content":"Client-mirror actions execute on the authority and return promises. UI that must read a result\nsynchronously — optimistic-free flows, render-phase reads of action results, hot paths where a\nround-trip is a regression — should keep authority local instead of forcing every read through\na transport."},"527":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use-15","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use#your-measured-update-hot-path-misses-its-budget","content":"Do not infer a universal write penalty from one microbenchmark. In the measured 4.0 scenario that\nupdates one item and then reads a derived total across 1,000 items, Coaction reaches about 55% of the\nthroughput of the equivalent Zustand selector case and is far behind a hand-maintained field. A\nseparate bulk benchmark shows that other update shapes can be comparable or favor Mutative. For\nhigh-frequency drag, animation frames, and streaming tick handlers, benchmark the representative\noperation and skip Coaction when it misses the required budget."},"528":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use-16","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use#you-need-an-ecosystem-that-already-exists","content":"Mature devtools, a large middleware shelf, community answers on every edge case. Coaction is a\nfocused project, not an ecosystem. Check the support matrix\nbefore betting a large surface on it."},"529":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use-17","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use#your-browser-matrix-punishes-sharedworker","content":"Module SharedWorkers are inconsistent across browsers and private modes. If every tab must share\none state instance, treat missing `SharedWorker` as a hard failure rather than shipping the\nlocal fallback and hoping. Cross-tab state that merely\nneeds to *eventually* agree often fits `BroadcastChannel` + persistence — simpler machinery,\nweaker guarantees."},"530":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use-18","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use#reach-for-coaction-when","content":"**One state, many tabs.** A SharedWorker authority with mirrored clients — the\ncross-tab todos demo\nreplays a full editing session across tabs on three engines."},"531":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use-19","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use#reach-for-coaction-when","content":"**Heavy compute off the main thread.** Keep the write authority in a Web Worker; the main\nthread keeps synchronous local reads from its mirror."},"532":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use-20","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use#reach-for-coaction-when","content":"**You want signals ergonomics without leaving the `create()` world.** Render tracking and\ncached computed values with Zustand-style stores."},"533":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use-21","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use#reach-for-coaction-when","content":"**Gradual adoption matters.** The Zustand adapter wraps an\nexisting store first; workers and cross-tab mode can come later without rewriting call sites."},"534":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use-22","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use#reach-for-coaction-when","content":"**Real-time collaboration.** The Yjs binding puts CRDT state behind\nthe same store interface."},"535":{"id":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use-23","page_id":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guides/when-not-to-use#a-rule-of-thumb","content":"> Adopt Coaction when the *shape of your problem* is more than one thread, more than one tab, or\n> more derivation than you want to memoize by hand. Adopt something smaller when it is not."},"536":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract","type":"page","content":"Shared JSON contract","breadcrumbs":["Coaction","Shared runtime"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract"},"537":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract-0","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract","content":"Know exactly which values may cross Coaction's worker, tab, and transport boundary."},"538":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract-1","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract#supported-values","content":"Supported values"},"539":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract-2","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract#rejected-values","content":"Rejected values"},"540":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract-3","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract#methods-and-getters-are-not-data","content":"Methods and getters are not data"},"541":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract-4","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract#model-common-values-explicitly","content":"Model common values explicitly"},"542":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract-5","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract#local-mode-is-different","content":"Local mode is different"},"543":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract-6","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract","content":"Every value crossing shared mode is encoded as JSON. Coaction validates values before they enter\nthe wire protocol rather than relying on `JSON.stringify()` to silently normalize them."},"544":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract-7","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract","content":"The rule applies to:"},"545":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract-8","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract","content":"initial shared state and full-sync snapshots;"},"546":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract-9","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract","content":"action arguments;"},"547":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract-10","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract","content":"non-void action results;"},"548":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract-11","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract","content":"patch values;"},"549":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract-12","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract","content":"replacement state carried by transport operations."},"550":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract-13","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract#supported-values","content":"A transported value must be a tree composed of:"},"551":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract-14","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract#supported-values","content":"`null`;"},"552":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract-15","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract#supported-values","content":"booleans and strings;"},"553":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract-16","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract#supported-values","content":"finite numbers other than negative zero;"},"554":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract-17","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract#supported-values","content":"dense arrays of supported values;"},"555":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract-18","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract#supported-values","content":"plain records with safe string keys and supported values."},"556":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract-19","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract#rejected-values","content":"Coaction rejects values that JSON cannot preserve without semantic loss:"},"557":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract-20","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract#rejected-values","content":"Category"},"558":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract-21","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract#rejected-values","content":"Examples"},"559":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract-22","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract#rejected-values","content":"Missing/non-JSON primitives"},"560":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract-23","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract#rejected-values","content":"`undefined`, `BigInt`, symbols"},"561":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract-24","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract#rejected-values","content":"Non-finite or normalized numbers"},"562":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract-25","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract#rejected-values","content":"`NaN`, `Infinity`, `-Infinity`, `-0`"},"563":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract-26","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract#rejected-values","content":"Runtime behavior in data"},"564":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract-27","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract#rejected-values","content":"functions, accessors"},"565":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract-28","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract#rejected-values","content":"Non-plain platform objects"},"566":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract-29","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract#rejected-values","content":"`Date`, `URL`, `Map`, `Set`, typed arrays, DOM objects"},"567":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract-30","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract#rejected-values","content":"Ambiguous graphs"},"568":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract-31","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract#rejected-values","content":"circular references, repeated references to the same object"},"569":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract-32","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract#rejected-values","content":"Non-dense arrays"},"570":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract-33","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract#rejected-values","content":"sparse arrays or arrays with extra enumerable properties"},"571":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract-34","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract#rejected-values","content":"Unsafe keys/paths"},"572":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract-35","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract#rejected-values","content":"`__proto__`, `prototype`, `constructor` in protected patch paths"},"573":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract-36","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract#rejected-values","content":"Repeated references are rejected even if `JSON.stringify()` would duplicate them. A tree does\nnot preserve object identity, so accepting aliases would make the authority and client graphs\nobservably different."},"574":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract-37","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract#methods-and-getters-are-not-data","content":"Store methods and computed accessors remain runtime behavior. Coaction extracts pure state for\ntransport, then materializes the methods and getters declared by the local source on each side."},"575":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract-38","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract#methods-and-getters-are-not-data","content":"Do not place a function inside a data object and expect it to behave like an action."},"576":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract-39","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract#model-common-values-explicitly","content":"Convert the value at the application boundary and give it a stable domain representation."},"577":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract-40","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract#local-mode-is-different","content":"The strict JSON contract applies only when state crosses a shared boundary. A local store may\nhold richer application values, subject to the normal immutable state model. If a store might\nmove into a worker later, keeping its data JSON-shaped from the beginning makes that migration\npredictable."},"578":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract-41","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/json-contract#local-mode-is-different","content":"Shared mode intentionally fails closed. If a value is not a lossless JSON\ntree, model or encode it explicitly instead of bypassing transport validation."},"579":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/overview","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/overview","type":"page","content":"Shared runtime overview","breadcrumbs":["Coaction","Shared runtime"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/shared/overview"},"580":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/overview-0","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/overview","content":"Use one authority and any number of local mirrors across Workers, SharedWorkers, or custom transports."},"581":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/overview-1","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/shared/overview#move-the-same-source","content":"Move the same source"},"582":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/overview-2","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/shared/overview#what-the-runtime-handles","content":"What the runtime handles"},"583":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/overview-3","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/shared/overview#what-the-application-still-owns","content":"What the application still owns"},"584":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/overview-4","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/shared/overview#middleware-placement","content":"Middleware placement"},"585":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/overview-5","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/overview","content":"Coaction shared mode keeps a single mutation authority. A Worker, SharedWorker, or custom\ntransport can host the main store; page runtimes hold client mirrors."},"586":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/overview-6","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/overview","content":"Clients are not peers. They can read local mirrored state, subscribe to it, and call methods that\nexecute on the authority. They cannot create an independent write path with `setState()`."},"587":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/overview-7","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/overview#move-the-same-source","content":"Keep the state factory in a module shared by the authority and clients:"},"588":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/overview-8","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/overview#move-the-same-source","content":"Create it in a worker:"},"589":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/overview-9","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/overview#move-the-same-source","content":"Connect from the page:"},"590":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/overview-10","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/overview#move-the-same-source","content":"On the page, `increment()` returns a promise:"},"591":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/overview-11","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/overview#move-the-same-source","content":"TypeScript models this client shape with `StoreWithAsyncFunction`/`Asyncify`: methods become\npromise-returning while data fields remain readable from the local mirror."},"592":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/overview-12","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/overview#what-the-runtime-handles","content":"action discovery and remote method execution;"},"593":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/overview-13","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/overview#what-the-runtime-handles","content":"strict JSON encoding and message-shape validation;"},"594":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/overview-14","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/overview#what-the-runtime-handles","content":"monotonically ordered patch updates within an authority epoch;"},"595":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/overview-15","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/overview#what-the-runtime-handles","content":"duplicate suppression and gap detection;"},"596":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/overview-16","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/overview#what-the-runtime-handles","content":"atomic full-snapshot recovery;"},"597":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/overview-17","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/overview#what-the-runtime-handles","content":"reconnect generation isolation;"},"598":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/overview-18","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/overview#what-the-runtime-handles","content":"rejection of responses from a superseded authority."},"599":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/overview-19","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/overview#what-the-application-still-owns","content":"choosing the Worker/SharedWorker lifetime;"},"600":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/overview-20","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/overview#what-the-application-still-owns","content":"designing idempotent actions or application-level deduplication;"},"601":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/overview-21","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/overview#what-the-application-still-owns","content":"authorization policy for requests reaching the authority;"},"602":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/overview-22","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/overview#what-the-application-still-owns","content":"keeping every connected runtime on the same Coaction major;"},"603":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/overview-23","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/overview#what-the-application-still-owns","content":"ensuring state, arguments, and results obey the JSON contract."},"604":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/overview-24","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/overview#middleware-placement","content":"Persistence, history, and Yjs belong on the owning main store. They mutate or merge state and\nare rejected on a client mirror. Logger can run on either side, but a client logger observes\nmirror updates and proxied calls rather than hidden authority-side work."},"605":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/overview-25","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/overview#middleware-placement","content":"See workers and reconnect for multi-tab setup, epochs, and in-flight\naction behavior."},"606":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect","type":"page","content":"Workers, policies, and reconnect","breadcrumbs":["Coaction","Shared runtime"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect"},"607":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect-0","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect","content":"Configure Worker and SharedWorker clients, restrict authority actions, and handle epoch changes safely."},"608":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect-1","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect#dedicated-worker","content":"Dedicated Worker"},"609":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect-2","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect#sharedworker-across-tabs","content":"SharedWorker across tabs"},"610":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect-3","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect#restrict-the-authority-surface","content":"Restrict the authority surface"},"611":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect-4","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect#epochs-and-sequence-recovery","content":"Epochs and sequence recovery"},"612":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect-5","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect#awaiting-action-visibility","content":"Awaiting action visibility"},"613":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect-6","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect#authority-changes-during-an-action","content":"Authority changes during an action"},"614":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect-7","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect#dedicated-worker","content":"A dedicated Worker gives one page its own authority lifetime:"},"615":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect-8","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect#dedicated-worker","content":"Destroy the Coaction store when the client no longer owns the connection. Terminate the Worker\naccording to your application's ownership model."},"616":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect-9","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect#sharedworker-across-tabs","content":"A reusable module can create a SharedWorker in page runtimes and become the authority inside the\nworker runtime:"},"617":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect-10","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect#sharedworker-across-tabs","content":"Each tab gets a client mirror while the SharedWorker owns one state instance. Passing the explicit\n`worker` key with an `undefined` value degrades to a local authority. Its `getState()` actions still\nreturn promises and its state, action arguments, and action results obey the shared JSON contract,\nso awaited call sites remain portable between modes."},"618":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect-11","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect#sharedworker-across-tabs","content":"Degraded tabs run independent local state. If every tab must see the same state, treat a missing\nSharedWorker as a hard error instead of relying on the fallback. The degraded store has\n`share === false` and owns its state locally, so its low-level `setState()` and `apply()` methods\nremain available. Always invoke actions through `getState()` and await them before reading their\neffects."},"619":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect-12","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect#sharedworker-across-tabs","content":"Coaction cannot catch an exception thrown while your code evaluates `new SharedWorker(...)` before\n`create()` is called. Catch that constructor failure yourself only when local fallback is an\nacceptable product decision. A worker or transport that exists but fails during setup is surfaced\nas an error rather than silently changing the authority model."},"620":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect-13","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect#restrict-the-authority-surface","content":"The authority only exposes method paths discovered from its store. `transportPolicy` can narrow\nthat surface further:"},"621":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect-14","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect#restrict-the-authority-surface","content":"`allowedActions` is an allowlist of method paths."},"622":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect-15","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect#restrict-the-authority-surface","content":"`authorize` receives a decoded JSON execute or full-sync request."},"623":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect-16","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect#restrict-the-authority-surface","content":"`mapError` may return a deliberately client-visible message."},"624":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect-17","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect#restrict-the-authority-surface","content":"Unexpected action errors are redacted to `Remote action failed`. The original error remains on\nthe authority. Treat policy code as trusted application code and keep it side-effect free where\npossible."},"625":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect-18","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect#epochs-and-sequence-recovery","content":"Each authority lifetime owns a unique epoch and a sequence that begins at zero. A client:"},"626":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect-19","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect#epochs-and-sequence-recovery","content":"fetches an atomic `{ epoch, sequence, state }` snapshot;"},"627":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect-20","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect#epochs-and-sequence-recovery","content":"applies only the next sequence for that epoch;"},"628":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect-21","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect#epochs-and-sequence-recovery","content":"ignores duplicate or older updates;"},"629":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect-22","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect#epochs-and-sequence-recovery","content":"requests a full snapshot after a sequence gap or epoch change."},"630":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect-23","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect#epochs-and-sequence-recovery","content":"Snapshot replacement is atomic. A failed validation or apply step leaves the client's previous\nepoch, sequence, and state intact."},"631":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect-24","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect#awaiting-action-visibility","content":"An action response includes the authority epoch and resulting sequence. The client waits for its\nmirror to catch up before resolving the action promise. If the incremental update does not arrive\nwithin `executeSyncTimeoutMs` (default `1500` ms), the client falls back to full sync."},"632":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect-25","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect#awaiting-action-visibility","content":"Increase the timeout only when legitimate worker execution and message scheduling routinely\nexceed the default. It is not a replacement for fixing a broken transport."},"633":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect-26","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect#authority-changes-during-an-action","content":"If the authority changes while an action is in flight, a response from the old epoch rejects with\n`ActionAuthorityChangedError`."},"634":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect-27","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect#authority-changes-during-an-action","content":"Its `outcome` is `unknown`: the old authority may already have performed the action. Retry only\nwhen the action is idempotent or protected by an application-level idempotency key."},"635":{"id":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect-28","page_id":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shared/workers-and-reconnect#authority-changes-during-an-action","content":"Reconnect callbacks are generation-scoped, so a late callback from an older connection cannot\noverwrite state established by a newer one."},"636":{"id":"/en/docs/reference/contributing","page_id":"/en/docs/reference/contributing","type":"page","content":"Contributing","breadcrumbs":["Coaction","Reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference/contributing"},"637":{"id":"/en/docs/reference/contributing-0","page_id":"/en/docs/reference/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference/contributing","content":"Navigate the repository, run the quality gates, and extend adapters without weakening maintained contracts."},"638":{"id":"/en/docs/reference/contributing-1","page_id":"/en/docs/reference/contributing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference/contributing#repository-map","content":"Repository map"},"639":{"id":"/en/docs/reference/contributing-2","page_id":"/en/docs/reference/contributing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference/contributing#quality-commands","content":"Quality commands"},"640":{"id":"/en/docs/reference/contributing-3","page_id":"/en/docs/reference/contributing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference/contributing#add-an-external-adapter","content":"Add an external adapter"},"641":{"id":"/en/docs/reference/contributing-4","page_id":"/en/docs/reference/contributing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference/contributing#change-shared-behavior-carefully","content":"Change shared behavior carefully"},"642":{"id":"/en/docs/reference/contributing-5","page_id":"/en/docs/reference/contributing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/reference/contributing#pull-request-ci","content":"Pull request CI"},"643":{"id":"/en/docs/reference/contributing-6","page_id":"/en/docs/reference/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference/contributing","content":"Read the repository's\nCONTRIBUTING.md,\nCode of Conduct, and\nSecurity Policy before opening a\nchange. Report vulnerabilities through the security process, not a public issue."},"644":{"id":"/en/docs/reference/contributing-7","page_id":"/en/docs/reference/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference/contributing#repository-map","content":"`packages/core`: local/shared creation, state materialization, patch flow, transports, adapter\nhooks, and lifecycle;"},"645":{"id":"/en/docs/reference/contributing-8","page_id":"/en/docs/reference/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference/contributing#repository-map","content":"`packages/coaction-*`: framework wrappers, whole-store adapters, middleware, and Yjs;"},"646":{"id":"/en/docs/reference/contributing-9","page_id":"/en/docs/reference/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference/contributing#repository-map","content":"`examples`: runnable framework, adapter, shared-worker, middleware, and collaboration examples;"},"647":{"id":"/en/docs/reference/contributing-10","page_id":"/en/docs/reference/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference/contributing#repository-map","content":"`docs`: architecture contracts, generated API, comparisons, migration, and benchmark notes;"},"648":{"id":"/en/docs/reference/contributing-11","page_id":"/en/docs/reference/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference/contributing#repository-map","content":"`apps/website`: this static Fumadocs site."},"649":{"id":"/en/docs/reference/contributing-12","page_id":"/en/docs/reference/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference/contributing#quality-commands","content":"Run the focused package test while iterating, then the relevant repository gates before handing\noff the change. Generated core API docs are checked with:"},"650":{"id":"/en/docs/reference/contributing-13","page_id":"/en/docs/reference/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference/contributing#quality-commands","content":"This freshness check also runs in `pnpm check` and CI. It does not check hand-written\nsemantics or catalog completeness. README, repository guides and the website's two languages\nare separate sources; update matching claims and examples together. The\ndocumentation map\nlists the related surfaces and website checks."},"651":{"id":"/en/docs/reference/contributing-14","page_id":"/en/docs/reference/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference/contributing#add-an-external-adapter","content":"First choose the right integration family:"},"652":{"id":"/en/docs/reference/contributing-15","page_id":"/en/docs/reference/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference/contributing#add-an-external-adapter","content":"framework wrapper: reactive/lifecycle binding for a UI framework;"},"653":{"id":"/en/docs/reference/contributing-16","page_id":"/en/docs/reference/contributing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/reference/contributing#add-an-external-adapter","content":"whole-store adapter: an external run