ld or\nthe scan's result through a selector, which re-renders only when its result changes. Objects\nreached through object keys are tracked as before."],[619,"Coaction cannot catch an exception thrown while your code evaluates `new SharedWorker(...)` before\n`create()` is called. Catch that constructor failure yourself only when local fallback is an\nacceptable product decision. A worker or transport that exists but fails during setup is surfaced\nas an error rather than silently changing the authority model."],[411,"Coaction deliberately keeps a familiar `create()` shape, but a migration is more than changing\nan import. Move one behavior at a time and keep tests green between steps."],[1,"Coaction documentation"],[432,"Coaction does not currently promise a Redux DevTools-compatible built-in experience. Keep\nproject-specific diagnostics or use logger until a maintained DevTools surface exists."],[165,"Coaction exposes a readonly public state. Actions may read through `this`, but all writes to\nCoaction-owned state must happen inside `set()`:"],[6,"Coaction is a Zustand-style state library with three pieces designed to work as one system:"],[15,"Coaction is most useful when an application has selector-heavy components, repeated derived\nstate, or a likely path toward worker-backed state. Instead of assembling independent tracking,\ncomputed, immutable-update, and selector plugins, Coaction connects those concerns through one\nreactive graph."],[421,"Coaction path"],[168,"Coaction records the public shape during initialization. A single store cannot add unknown\ntop-level keys later. A slice store cannot add new slices or new top-level fields inside a\nslice."],[556,"Coaction rejects values that JSON cannot preserve without semantic loss:"],[44,"Coaction requires Node.js 22 or newer for repository development. Published runtime packages are\ninstalled from npm with the package manager you already use."],[585,"Coaction shared mode keeps a single mutation authority. 